00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:41,040
Of course they're negotiated.

256
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:42,520
They've been obliterated.

257
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:43,900
Who wouldn't negotiate?

258
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:46,240
They are begging to make a deal.

259
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:48,900
We'll see if we can make the right deal.

260
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:54,100
And if they make the right deal, then the straight will open up.

261
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:55,760
Haramu's straight will open up.

262
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:58,560
And even now, we don't know if there are any mines.

263
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:02,860
You know, they have 22 mine — they call mine droppers.

264
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:05,280
Think of it. Who would have 22 mine droppers?

265
00:13:05,380 --> 00:13:07,020
This is a boat that drops mines.

266
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:12,760
Who has 22 mine droppers except for people with very evil intention?

267
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:17,440
So every one of those mine droppers has been struck.

268
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:26,520
We're the same weapon we used to stop drugs from coming into the United States of America.

269
00:13:27,260 --> 00:13:30,760
When we hit those boats, it's the exact same weapon, extremely effective.

270
00:13:30,760 --> 00:13:37,080
We have unlimited supplies and extremely effective, but they have no more mine drivers.

271
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:45,220
By the way, speaking of drugs, we're 98 percent down drugs coming in by water, by the ocean,

272
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:46,140
by the sea.

273
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:54,060
And we're trying to find out who are the 2% because we think they're the bravest men anywhere in the world.

274
00:13:54,280 --> 00:13:55,880
Maybe women.

275
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:59,960
But whoever's on those boats is very brave or doesn't watch television.

276
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:06,560
But where drugs coming in by sea, coming in by water, are 98% down.

277
00:14:07,420 --> 00:14:09,300
And now we'll stop the drugs coming in by land.

278
00:14:09,340 --> 00:14:13,180
The land is the easy one. You had to stop the water. A lot of it came in through the water.

279
00:14:13,180 --> 00:14:17,760
Now it's all pinched and these people are trying to come in by land.

280
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:20,200
And we will — that's it.

281
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,440
That's the easy one.

282
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:23,400
But we had to take care of the water for us.

283
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:25,080
Nobody's — nobody's coming.

284
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:27,660
Very — virtually nothing is coming in anymore.

285
00:14:28,180 --> 00:14:31,960
It was hundreds of millions of dollars a week

286
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,560
were coming in by water.

287
00:14:34,400 --> 00:14:39,360
They now have the chance, that is, Iran,

288
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:41,840
to permanently abandon their nuclear ambitions

289
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:43,580
and to chart a new path forward.

290
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:45,060
We'll see if they want to do it.

291
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:48,040
If they don't, we're their worst nightmare.

292
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:49,640
In the meantime, we'll just keep

293
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:54,960
blowing them away, unimpeded, unstopped.

294
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:57,080
Well, there's not a thing they can do about it.

295
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:58,840
They can't do anything about it, you know.

296
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:00,260
I tell you if they could, if they could,

297
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:01,400
you'd be hearing about it.

298
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:03,300
You'd be hearing about it.

299
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:05,300
You don't hear anything about it.

300
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:06,820
They can't shoot our jets.

301
00:15:06,820 --> 00:15:08,900
We have the best — we have the best military

302
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:11,560
equipment in the world, not even a contest.

303
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:13,900
You see that with Venezuela?

304
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:15,600
They had other equipment.

305
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:16,380
They didn't have ours.

306
00:15:16,380 --> 00:15:17,020
It didn't work.

307
00:15:17,820 --> 00:15:18,320
It didn't work.

308
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:18,760
Think of it.

309
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:22,060
We did a — the situation in Venezuela.

310
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:27,820
military operation, getting a very, very dangerous man who's killed a lot of people,

311
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:29,820
forced people into our country.

312
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:31,260
Incredible.

313
00:15:31,740 --> 00:15:36,440
He emptied his prisons in Venezuela, emptied his prisons into our country,

314
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:39,660
and I hope that charge will be brought at some point,

315
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:42,400
because that was a big charge that hasn't been brought yet.

316
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:44,680
It should be brought.

317
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:46,940
He emptied his prisons into our country

318
00:15:47,620 --> 00:15:52,060
and was a major purveyor of drugs coming into our country.

319
00:15:52,740 --> 00:16:00,960
And he's now been captured and he'll, you know, I guess be given a fair trial.

320
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:04,520
But I would imagine there are other trials coming because they have just,

321
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:09,560
they've really sued him just in a fraction of the kind of things that he's done.

322
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:12,360
Other cases are going to be broad, as you probably know.

323
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:17,580
In the meantime, with Iran, we're going to keep doing what we've been doing.

324
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:22,600
And nobody's a match for the United States, but they're not a match for the United States.

325
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:24,620
It's small potatoes. That's why.

326
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:29,180
I'm so disappointed in NATO because this was a test for NATO.

327
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:30,300
This was a test.

328
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:31,060
You can help us.

329
00:16:31,060 --> 00:16:32,100
You don't have to.

330
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:35,760
But if you don't have — you know, if you don't do that, we're going to remember.

331
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:37,180
Just remember.

332
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:40,000
Remember this in a number of months from now.

333
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,180
Remember my statements.

334
00:16:43,520 --> 00:16:48,400
They have an expression, a great expression, never forget.

335
00:16:48,660 --> 00:16:49,500
You can never forget.

336
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:56,240
So, as we end threats to America abroad, we're focused here at home on building the greatest

337
00:16:56,540 --> 00:16:58,220
economy and the history of the world.

338
00:16:58,220 --> 00:17:00,940
Now, before this started, the Dow hit 50,000.

339
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:03,780
The S&P hit 7,000.

340
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:10,140
Both of those achievements were not achievable.

341
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:16,280
Every one of you, most of you, I guess, said you'll never hit 50,000 during a four-year

342
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:18,840
period because it was too high a number.

343
00:17:18,840 --> 00:17:20,360
Well, we hit it in our first year.

344
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:29,100
And I said, well, now we have to take an excursion to Iran and we have to stop this maniac who's no longer with us.

345
00:17:30,020 --> 00:17:33,920
The supreme leader wasn't so supreme, no longer with us.

346
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:34,820
It's very sad.

347
00:17:35,220 --> 00:17:41,280
But we have to stop him from blowing up the world, blowing up the Middle East and blowing up our country.

348
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:42,560
And we did that.

349
00:17:44,640 --> 00:17:46,920
And I thought, frankly, I thought the oil prices would...

350
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:50,820
go up more, and I thought the stock market would go down more.

351
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:53,440
It hasn't been nearly as severe as I thought.

352
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:56,240
I think they have confidence in maybe the American president

353
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:58,840
and maybe the people sitting around this table.

354
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:02,800
But Americans filing their taxes this year are receiving

355
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:04,780
record-setting refunds.

356
00:18:04,820 --> 00:18:06,260
It's been a very big story.

357
00:18:06,260 --> 00:18:07,080
Well, it should be a big story.

358
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:10,100
I don't think you write about it that much, but I speak about it.

359
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:12,860
You know, I speak about it.

360
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,800
Because if I speak about it, at least people here,

361
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:15,700
you don't write about it.

362
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:20,720
You don't write about the drug prices going down.

363
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:24,940
It'll be going down 30, 40, 50, 60 percent, 70 percent.

364
00:18:26,180 --> 00:18:28,880
Favorite nations, call most favorite nations.

365
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,940
We're going to be paying the lowest price anywhere in the world

366
00:18:30,940 --> 00:18:34,180
before we paid the highest price in the world, Bobby, right?

367
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:36,700
And now we're going to pay the lowest price in the world.

368
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:38,060
That's quite a difference.

369
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:44,280
It's a difference from 40 to 70 and 80 and even 90 percent.

370
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:45,520
That's a pretty big difference.

371
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:51,420
But we're slashing regulations, and investment is pouring in from all over the world.

372
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:57,700
And we have the most investment of any country in history has been put into our country in the last year.

373
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:59,440
And again, we had to take a little detour.

374
00:19:00,060 --> 00:19:01,080
Won't be long.

375
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:03,020
It's going to end soon.

376
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:05,160
We had to take a little detour.

377
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:07,600
Go to Iran.

378
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:09,340
And we had to put out a fire.

379
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:14,380
Very dangerous fire that could have blown up big portions of the world, if not the whole thing.

380
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:19,860
So, tomorrow we'll be announcing a variety of actions that were taken to support American

381
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:21,420
farmers.

382
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:22,360
We never forget.

383
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:23,220
We love the farmers.

384
00:19:23,220 --> 00:19:26,820
We gave them $12 billion out of tariff money.

385
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:31,500
We had a tremendous amount of tariff money come in, and we continue to have.

386
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:35,440
We've gone, as you know, the Supreme Court gave us a very unfortunate, foolish ruling,

387
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:40,680
a ruling that gives people that have ripped off our country for many years, gives them

388
00:19:40,860 --> 00:19:41,740
some money back.

389
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:44,260
But it's one of those things.

390
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:45,480
It's a terrible, terrible...

391
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:51,340
horrible mistake they made, but it's okay because we have another method that's just as good.

392
00:19:51,340 --> 00:19:57,500
We'll use the other method. But because the tariff money has been so substantial, we gave our farmers

393
00:19:57,720 --> 00:20:05,600
who have been mistreated by some countries, we gave them $12 billion and they're extremely

394
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:10,860
happy and they deserve it. They've been great. They never complain. They just go out and

395
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:14,740
they farm and they wouldn't do anything different. They wouldn't trade jobs.

396
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:18,540
with any of you, except maybe some of the fake media.

397
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:19,000
I don't know.

398
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:20,280
Somehow I don't see that.

399
00:20:20,280 --> 00:20:22,660
I like their job better, actually.

400
00:20:23,060 --> 00:20:24,040
I love the farmers.

401
00:20:24,300 --> 00:20:25,320
So we gave them $12 billion.

402
00:20:26,420 --> 00:20:31,600
So in just a few moments, Treasury Secretary Scott Besant will discuss the actions that

403
00:20:31,620 --> 00:20:37,340
we're taking to address energy prices, which have not gone up as much as I thought, Scott,

404
00:20:37,380 --> 00:20:38,400
to be honest with you.

405
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:42,280
And, you know, it's not over, so maybe it'll go up a little bit more.

406
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:45,100
It's all going to come back down to where it was and probably lower.

407
00:20:45,700 --> 00:20:47,340
And my predictions have been right.

408
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:48,660
Trump was right about everything.

409
00:20:48,660 --> 00:20:49,440
They have a new hat.

410
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:51,240
Trump was right about everything.

411
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:53,700
It's pretty right.

412
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:57,500
But Scott's going to address that.

413
00:20:57,880 --> 00:21:01,360
And I think before we go very much further, I want to

414
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:04,780
ask Vice President J.D. Vance to say a few words about

415
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:08,960
where we are with the situation.

416
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:11,580
He's involved with Steve and with Jared on negotiations.

417
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,480
And then some of the others will speak.

418
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:15,820
We'll have Marco say a few words.

419
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:19,880
Pete Hagset, who was born for this role.

420
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:22,420
I mean, he's doing a great job.

421
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:23,860
They gave him a hard time.

422
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:26,260
And now people, I'll tell you, somebody came up to me

423
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:28,120
yesterday, gave you a very hard time, said, you know,

424
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:28,820
I made a mistake.

425
00:21:29,360 --> 00:21:31,500
Pete Hanks at this doing a good job.

426
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:34,800
So when I tell you who, you're not even going to believe it.

427
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:38,800
He said, Hanks, he gave you such a nasty hard time.

428
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:40,640
But you're doing great.

429
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:47,640
And then Steve is going to speak, and Scott will speak last.

430
00:21:47,940 --> 00:21:50,780
And if we have any questions, we'll take some questions.

431
00:21:50,860 --> 00:21:51,880
You may have questions.

432
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:53,520
I doubt it, but you may ask.

433
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:56,000
So, JD, please.

434
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:56,500
Yes, sir.

435
00:21:56,500 --> 00:21:57,140
Well, thank you.

436
00:21:57,140 --> 00:21:58,820
It's good to see everybody.

437
00:21:58,820 --> 00:22:01,280
Proud to be part of this team, proud to be serving the President of the country.

438
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:02,780
Let me just say a couple things.

439
00:22:02,780 --> 00:22:06,700
The first of all is the President summarized this very ably.

440
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:10,340
But look, the Iranian conventional military is effectively destroyed.

441
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:12,300
They don't have a navy.

442
00:22:12,340 --> 00:22:15,080
They don't have the ability to hit us like they could have even a few weeks ago.

443
00:22:15,080 --> 00:22:17,660
What that does is that gives us options, Mr. President.

444
00:22:17,860 --> 00:22:21,900
Now there's been a lot of reporting about diplomatic options, about negotiations.

445
00:22:21,900 --> 00:22:23,560
There's of course Pete and his team.

446
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:25,400
There are further military options.

447
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:29,560
But what we have now that we didn't have when the president took over just a little over

448
00:22:29,660 --> 00:22:36,080
a year ago is the ability to use every tool at our disposal to ensure that Iran doesn't

449
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:37,060
get a nuclear weapon.

450
00:22:37,080 --> 00:22:42,000
Because when I say options, I think it's important the American people know options for what.

451
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:45,100
And it's options to ensure that Iran never has a nuclear weapon.

452
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:49,160
You talk about people who walk into a crowded supermarket and have a vest on.

453
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:52,820
And they blow up the vest and a couple of people get killed and that's a terrible tragedy.

454
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:54,060
What happens when what's on the vest?

455
00:22:54,180 --> 00:22:59,580
It's not something that can kill a couple of people but can kill many, many tens of thousands of people.

456
00:22:59,600 --> 00:23:05,660
That is the most important American national security objective that exists for any administration at any time

457
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:08,720
is you don't want the worst people in the world to have a nuclear weapon.

458
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:10,920
That's why the president is doing this.

459
00:23:11,060 --> 00:23:14,000
That's why the president cares so much about this particular issue.

460
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:17,800
I'll let Steve talk a little bit about the details of the negotiation.

461
00:23:18,220 --> 00:23:21,200
But the last thing I'll say before I turn it over to Marco is,

462
00:23:21,220 --> 00:23:27,160
I'm very mindful, of course, that we have a lot of folks overseas fighting very ably for the United States of America.

463
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:34,160
I know Pete and the whole team were very proud of them, but they're fighting at a time where we are about to enter as Christians

464
00:23:34,700 --> 00:23:41,320
the most important week of the Christian calendar, the Holy Week that celebrates the return of Jesus Christ to Jerusalem.

465
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:46,720
And so I want to say to all of my fellow American Christians, but particularly those serving in the Gulf,

466
00:23:46,760 --> 00:23:54,980
that I wish you all a very blessed Easter, a very blessed Holy Week, and we continue to stand behind you and continue to support you every step of the way.

467
00:23:55,060 --> 00:23:55,340
Thank you, sir.

468
00:23:55,340 --> 00:23:56,700
Thank you very much.

469
00:23:57,120 --> 00:23:57,700
Michael?

470
00:23:58,020 --> 00:24:02,300
The most important job any president has is to keep the American people safe.

471
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:05,380
And every president says it, but we have a president that means it and does something

472
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:06,300
about it.

473
00:24:06,300 --> 00:24:10,900
As the president outlined very clearly to the world on the night this operation began,

474
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:14,800
Iran has been at war with the United States for 47 years.

475
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:19,360
For 47 years, Iran has been killing Americans and attacking Americans across this planet.

476
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:22,080
And other presidents had an opportunity to do something about it.

477
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:25,060
And they all warned about how Iran was dangerous, but they refused to act.

478
00:24:25,060 --> 00:24:27,480
And this president's not someone that's going to refuse to act.

479
00:24:27,480 --> 00:24:29,860
He's not going to leave a danger like this in place.

480
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:32,200
He's going to address it, and that is what he is doing.

481
00:24:32,700 --> 00:24:35,920
From the very first night of this operation, the president made it very clear.

482
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:39,760
People like this, and now what I'm talking about is not the people of Iran.

483
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:42,560
The people that run this country are radical Shia clerics.

484
00:24:42,560 --> 00:24:44,620
These are religious fanatics.

485
00:24:44,620 --> 00:24:46,860
Look what they are doing now at their weakest point.

486
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:48,880
This is the weakest Iran has ever been.

487
00:24:48,880 --> 00:24:50,060
And look at what they're doing.

488
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:51,640
They're attacking embassies.

489
00:24:51,860 --> 00:24:54,460
They're attacking hotels.

490
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:57,420
Imagine what these people would do if they had a nuclear weapon.

491
00:24:57,420 --> 00:25:00,100
That is an unacceptable risk for the world.

492
00:25:00,260 --> 00:25:03,640
By the way, the president's not just doing a favor to the United States and to our people.

493
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:04,960
This is for the world.

494
00:25:05,220 --> 00:25:09,300
He defined very clearly on the first night of this operation what the goal was.

495
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:12,760
We were going to destroy Iran's Navy, and that is happening.

